---
const paths = [
  { title: 'Build a foundation', description: 'Component state, lifecycle, forms, draft editing, localization, themes, and keyboard-friendly controls.' },
  { title: 'Work with data', description: 'Deterministic grids, server paging, typed HTTP clients, cancellation, SQLite migrations, and concurrency.' },
  { title: 'Explore boundaries', description: 'Demo identities and policies, atomic CSV imports, bounded uploads, and cancellable server work.' },
  { title: 'Observe and deliver', description: 'Trace IDs, health checks, behavior tests, Docker, dependency and container scanning, and hosting considerations.' },
];
---
<section class="dashboard" aria-labelledby="paths-title">
  <p class="section-kicker">Explore the toolbox</p>
  <h2 id="paths-title">Practical patterns with their tradeoffs visible</h2>
  <div class="features-grid">{paths.map(path => <article class="feature-card"><h3>{path.title}</h3><p>{path.description}</p></article>)}</div>
</section>
<section class="quickstart-section" aria-labelledby="quickstart-title">
  <div class="quickstart-copy">
    <p class="section-kicker">Start locally</p>
    <h2 id="quickstart-title">A classroom that fits in one application</h2>
    <p>No cloud account needed for the basic labs. Synthetic datasets reset on demand. A local notebook keeps your learning notes.</p>
    <a class="btn btn-text" href="./docs/getting-started/">Read the setup guide</a>
  </div>
  <div class="code-block"><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/jonathanperis/blazor-mudblazor-starter.git
cd blazor-mudblazor-starter
dotnet restore --locked-mode
dotnet run --project src/WebClient</code></pre></div>
</section>
